  "definition": "In this context, FDA refers to the regulatory body whose approval process and expedited programs are used to speed the development and review of therapies for serious conditions with unmet medical need. Its approval timing can vary depending on both the mix of expedited pathways used and the type of pivotal evidence submitted.",
